# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Mirrors .vercelignore, for the same reason and with one syntax difference
# that matters. Before this list, `COPY . .` sent roughly 73 GB to the daemon:
# datasets/ is 37 GB and tmp/ is 36 GB of MediaPipe extraction scratch. Both are
# gitignored, so neither shows up in a `git status` sanity check — the context
# is built from the working tree, not from git.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORING. Docker matches these against the path relative to the context
# root, so `models` names the top-level directory only. That is the behaviour
# this file depends on, because public/models MUST ship: it carries the served
# BiLSTM (model.json + weights.bin + labels.json) and the self-hosted MediaPipe
# .task and WASM. A leading slash makes the intent explicit rather than relying
# on a reader knowing the matching rule, and the negation below is belt and
# braces — if either the rule or this file is ever misread, public/models is
# still re-included.

# Dependencies and build output — the image installs and builds these itself
node_modules
.next
out

# 2.3 GB, and the build does not read it
.git
.gitignore

# Large data that is never served from the app bundle
datasets
/tmp
/models
.venv

# Tooling and analysis with no runtime role
scripts
docs
phases
coverage
e2e
tests
playwright-report
test-results
.agents
.claude
.vscode

# Secrets. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values arrive as build args instead — see Dockerfile.
.env
.env.*

# Editor and OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The served model and MediaPipe runtime must reach the image.
!public/models
